   "reference": {
    "title": "Functional vs non-functional PanNET & hereditary syndromes",
    "intro": "Functional classification is a clinical diagnosis (hormone hypersecretion syndrome) \u2014 hormone IHC positivity alone without a clinical syndrome does NOT make a PanNET functional.",
    "note": "ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Clinical syndromes & MEN1 / VHL clues",
      "points": [
       "Multifocal PanNETs or background microadenomatosis (< 5 mm microadenomas) strongly suggest MEN1, VHL, NF1, or TSC.",
       "Clear-cell lipid-rich PanNET is associated with VHL; psammomatous somatostatinoma in the periampullary duodenum is associated with NF1."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Pancreatic Neuroendocrine Tumour Syndromes",
